    "share_count_basis": "Common shares 323.560M + Operating Partnership limited-partner units 55.826M = 379.386M at 30-Jun-2026 (Q2-26 supplemental). UPREIT: FFO of the Operating Partnership accrues to common + LP units together, so the divisor includes both. Held flat.",
    "debt_memo": "Engine net_debt is 0 BY DESIGN: the capitalised stream (Real Estate FFO -> AFFO) is after interest, so subtracting debt would deduct it twice. Actual balance sheet for reference: total debt (our share) US$35,731M, consolidated cash US$1,019M at 30-Jun-2026; total debt / total assets 37% vs 65% covenant; Q2-26 secured financings at 5.36% weighted rate. Refinancing drag is carried in the margin path instead.",
    "fy0_construction": "FY2026E Real Estate FFO = guidance midpoint $13.25 x ~380M diluted units = US$5,035M; less straight-line rent ~US$50M (H1-26 $24.9M); less recurring capex (tenant allowances + operational capex, our share) ~US$640M (H1-26 $258.6M, H2 seasonally heavier) = cash AFFO US$4,345M after SBC; less equity-award taxes $14M = US$4,331M ($11.42/unit) house basis. Company FAD-style (SBC added back) = US$4,415M. FY2026E consolidated revenue US$7,220M = H1-26 actual $3,547.7M + H2 estimate (~$3,675M; Taubman consolidated from Q4-25). Engine mapping: 'EBITDA' = cash Real Estate FFO before SBC (70.2% of revenue), cash tax 0 (REIT; entity taxes already inside FFO), capex = recurring capex + SPG-share redevelopment spend, D&A irrelevant at 0% tax.",
    "wacc_rationale": "Cost of equity, not WACC (post-interest flow). 10y UST ~5.24% (2026-10-01) + 0.9 x 5.0% ERP = ~9.7%, rounded to 9.75% base. Set above O (9.5%) and PSA/MAA (9.0%) because SPG carries ~5.5x net debt/EBITDA, discretionary-retail tenant exposure and a fresh leadership transition. Bull 9.0%, bear 10.75%.",
    "lease_treatment": "SPG is the lessor; ground-lease expense sits inside property operating costs and therefore inside FFO. No separate lease charge.",
    "nci_treatment": "Real Estate FFO is 'our share' -- includes SPG's share of JV and Klepierre (equity-method) FFO and excludes consolidated NCI, so no NCI deduction. Taubman (TRG) consolidated from Q4-2025.",
    "notes": "MODEL: REIT AFFO capitalisation at cost of equity via the component engine (routing table row 'REIT / property trust'; same pattern as O, MAA, PSA). Net debt is never subtracted. Stream = Real Estate FFO (company definition: FFO excluding other platform investments -- Catalyst Brands/JCPenney/SPARC-type retail stakes -- and revaluation gains) minus straight-line rent, recurring capex and SBC/withholding. The platform investments are carried at ZERO value (their recent losses are excluded from the stream, their equity value is also excluded -- conservative net). Real Estate FFO per unit: H1-26 $6.46 (+7.5% y/y), Q2-26 $3.29 (+7.9%); FY2026 guide raised to $13.20-$13.30. GAAP EPS/net income are unusable as earnings (FY2025 NI $5,364M includes the Taubman remeasurement gain).",
